mipsstubs_noreturn_el.so, mipsstubs_noreturn_eb.so, mipsstubs_noreturn_n64el.so --
MIPS PIC shared objects whose imports are reached through .MIPS.stubs lazy
stubs (GH-904; kuna-cli/tests/mips_stub_noreturn.rs).

What they are
  Built from mipsstubs_noreturn.c with -nostdlib, so every libc call is an
  undefined import with a lazy stub (lw/ld $25,-0x7ff0($28); move $15,$31;
  jalr $25; li/daddiu $24,<dynsym index>). The linker lays the stubs out as
  memcpy, puts, abort, fopen, fclose, strcmp, exit, fputs, so memcpy and
  puts sit in front of abort's stub and fopen, fclose and strcmp in front
  of exit's.
  mipsstubs_noreturn_el.so    o32 little-endian
  mipsstubs_noreturn_eb.so    o32 big-endian
  mipsstubs_noreturn_n64el.so n64 little-endian (mips64r2; load with
                              --target MIPS:LE:64:default)

Why they are vendored
  CI has no MIPS toolchain, and the assertions depend on the stub order the
  linker chose.

Where they came from
  Ubuntu mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc 10.3.0, GNU ld 2.38 (host):

      mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -EL -mabi=32 -O2 -fPIC -shared -nostdlib \
          -Wl,--build-id=none mipsstubs_noreturn.c -o mipsstubs_noreturn_el.so
      mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -EB -mabi=32 -O2 -fPIC -shared -nostdlib \
          -Wl,--build-id=none mipsstubs_noreturn.c -o mipsstubs_noreturn_eb.so
      mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -EL -mabi=64 -march=mips64r2 -O2 -fPIC -shared \
          -nostdlib -Wl,--build-id=none mipsstubs_noreturn.c \
          -o mipsstubs_noreturn_n64el.so

  sha256:
    c11f94d55002ab777e079b009a21243794dd447aa12f24dafec5e38895345a78  mipsstubs_noreturn_el.so
    345cdb78cfd49b07e64aac144b9df911e37e8c1259f5bbceb41223cfdcb19d56  mipsstubs_noreturn_eb.so
    f25c7aac9f7679ea276b4bf1354ee1b95480838a7ccb5381b7d1973204c468c3  mipsstubs_noreturn_n64el.so
